<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Shaddadid Emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">951 CE – 1075 CE · capital Ganja</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Kurdish dynasty that ruled Ganja and Arran in the 10th and 11th centuries, a meeting point of Muslim, Armenian and Georgian worlds.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Shaddadids were a Kurdish family who exploited the decline of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-emirate">Sallarid Emirate</a>. In 951 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-shaddad">Muhammad ibn Shaddad</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dvin">Dvin</a>, and his descendants established their seat at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ganja-khanate">Ganja</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Arran</a>, taking over the region between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kura-river">Kura</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aras-river">Araxes</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> ruled a mixed population of Muslims and Christians and fought and allied in turn with the Armenian kings of Ani, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abul-aswar-shavur-i">Abu'l-Aswar Shavur</a>, who ruled from 1049, was a forceful soldier and patron. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ganja-khanate">Ganja</a> prospered as a market city on routes linking the Caspian, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> took control of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Arran</a>, and in 1075 the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik Shah</a> deposed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ganja-khanate">Ganja</a> line. A branch survived as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/shaddadids-of-ani">Shaddadids of Ani</a>, governing the former Armenian capital for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 951 CE – 1075 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Caucasus</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:78.63%;width:2.47%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>951 CE – 1075 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ganja</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn Shaddad, Fadl ibn Muhammad, Abu'l-Aswar Shavur</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian; Kurdish; Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>, <a href="/countries/armenia">Armenia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Shaddadids, Shaddadids of Ganja</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1013&amp;focus=shaddadid-emirate" aria-label="Shaddadid Emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5816 725 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Shaddadid Emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6136 981L6202 1060M6136 981L6481 1127M6136 981L6069 986"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6202 1060h0M6481 1127h0M6069 986h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6136 981h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6136 981h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ganja. <a href="/atlas?year=1013&amp;focus=shaddadid-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption>